CM_ "BMW E8x/E9x PT-CAN (powertrain CAN, 500 kbit/s) with MK60E5 DSC, all known frames. Generated by build_full_dbc.py. Reference: MK60E5 SPdaten (firmware tables, DSC_87.prg) and MEVD17.2 function description; verified against a 320i PT-CAN log and an E92 M3 K-CAN trace; secondary: E65_ReverseEngineering docs, NewTIS, superwofy frame notes, community DBC. See BMW_E9x_full_DBC_report.md";
CM_ BO_ 141 "DSC DTC D368: D368 - ELUP / vacuum system: PT_CAN message 8Dh STAT_ELUP invalid [DE: D368 - ELUP/Unterdrucksystem: PT_CAN Botschaft 8Dh STAT_ELUP ungueltig] (supervised: checksum, alive, timeout) | Not observed in the 320i PT-CAN log";
CM_ BO_ 168 "MK60E5 FW 7846816A (M3): DSC RX | MEVD17.2 BN2000: 'Drehmoment 1', sender DME, DME transmits, cycle 10 ms, DLC 8, variants [x x x x x] | DSC DTC D354: D354 - PT-CAN DME / DDE_1 - Torque 1 message 168 missing [DE: D354 - PT-CAN DME/DDE_1 - Drehmoment 1 Botschaft 168 fehlt] (supervised: checksum, alive, timeout) | E65 doc: 'Torque 1', DLC 8, cycle 10 ms | E65 message list: 'Drehmoment 1 K-CAN' from DME1/DDE1 | 320i log: 9382 frames, DLC 8 | cycle time source: BN2000";
CM_ SG_ 168 CHK_SUM_TORQ_1_DME "BMW 8-bit checksum: s = sum(other bytes) + (ID & 0xFF) + (ID >> 8); chk = (s & 0xFF) + (s >> 8) - verified 100 % in 320i log | previous name (community DBC): Checksum_EngineAndBrake | BMW name CHK_SUM_TORQ_1_DME - E65 doc (HeinrichG-V12/E65_ReverseEngineering, Bosch MED9.2.1)";
