CM_ BO_ 404 "Cruise-control stalk (SZL frame on F-CAN, copied to PT-CAN by the DSC's F-CAN -> PT-CAN gateway). Byte 2 (bits 16-23) is evaluated in priority order by BMW: 0xFF invalid; (b & 0x7F) == 0 no action; (b & 0xB0) == 0x10 tip down; (b & 0xB0) == 0x90 tip up; bit 6 axial tip; else low nibble 1 tip forward, 2 push forward, 4 tip back, 8 pull back (other values undefined) | E65 doc: 'Operation cruise control / ACC', DLC 4, cycle 200 ms | E65 message list: 'Bedienung Tempomat/ACC' from SZL_LWS | 320i log: 90 frames, DLC 4 | cycle time source: 320i log (estimated)";
CM_ SG_ 404 CHKSM_CCTR "BMW 8-bit checksum without ID: s = sum(other bytes) + 0; chk = (s & 0xFF) + (s >> 8) - verified 100 % in the 320i log and two E65 logs | previous name (community DBC): Checksum_404 | BMW name CHKSM_CCTR - E65 doc (HeinrichG-V12/E65_ReverseEngineering, Bosch MED9.2.1)";
CM_ SG_ 404 ALIV_CCTR "Message is sent at higher rate when cruise stalk is pressed | previous name (community DBC): Counter_404 | BMW name ALIV_CCTR - E65 doc (HeinrichG-V12/E65_ReverseEngineering, Bosch MED9.2.1)";
CM_ SG_ 404 OP_PUBU_CCTR_ACC "BMW name OP_PUBU_CCTR_ACC - E65 doc (HeinrichG-V12/E65_ReverseEngineering, Bosch MED9.2.1); one-hot enum; community DBC flags: bit 16 plus1mph, 17 plus5mph, 18 minus1mph, 19 minus5mph, 20 cancel, 22 resume; replaces Resume_request 22|1, Cancel_request_up_or_down_stalk 20|1, minus5mph_request 19|1, minus1mph_request 18|1, plus5mph_request 17|1, plus1mph_request 16|1 (community DBC ranks below E65) | bits 16|8: TASTER_TEMPOMAT_ACC - DSC_87.prg job STATUS_F_CAN_TEMPOMAT_ACC result STAT_TASTER_TEMPOMAT_ACC (ACC_Status aus F_CAN Telegramm); value table SGBD (0=Keine_Aktion; 1=Tippen_nach_vorne; 2=Ueberdruecken_nach_vorne; 4=Tippen_nach_hinten; 8=Ueberdruecken_nach_hinten; 16=Tippen_nach_unten; 64=Axial_Tippen; 144=Tippen_nach_oben; 255=Signal_ungueltig)";
CM_ SG_ 404 Cancel_request_up_stalk "Appears when cancel stalk (up) is depressed";
